-- Flow out of the reservoir into a numerical aquifer.  A row of eight oil
-- cells has a water injector in the last cell and a numerical aquifer of two
-- cells attached to the first.  The aquifer starts 20 bar below the
-- equilibrium pressure, so oil flows into the aquifer cells from the start,
-- while the connate water in the reservoir is immobile.  The injected water
-- later reaches the aquifer as well.  There is no producer.

RUNSPEC

TITLE
COMPOSITIONAL NUMERICAL AQUIFER TAKING FLUID FROM THE RESERVOIR

METRIC

OIL
GAS
WATER

DIMENS
10 1 1 /

COMPS
3 /

FULLIMP

TABDIMS
/

EQLDIMS
/

WELLDIMS
1 1 1 1 /

AQUDIMS
2 1 /

START
1 'JAN' 2020 /

UNIFOUT

GRID

INIT

DX
10*25 /
DY
10*50 /
DZ
10*10 /
TOPS
10*2000 /

PORO
10*0.25 /
PERMX
10*200 /
PERMY
10*200 /
PERMZ
10*200 /

-- Cells 9 and 10 become the aquifer.
AQUNUM
-- ID  I  J K  AREA    LENGTH  PORO  PERM  DEPTH  PRESSURE
   1   9  1 1  1.0E4   500     0.25  50    2020   180 /
   1   10 1 1  1.0E4   500     0.25  50    2030   180 /
/

AQUCON
-- ID  I1 I2 J1 J2 K1 K2  FACE  TRANMULT
   1   1  1  1  1  1  1   'I-'  0.5 /
/

